{
  "id": "lords-paradox",
  "term": "Lord’s paradox",
  "definition": "Lord’s paradox refers to a misleading result that can appear when researchers study change from pretest to posttest while statistically adjusting for the pretest score. If the predictor is related to initial scores and those scores contain random error, this adjustment can create a regression-to-the-mean artifact that makes a variable seem to predict improvement when it may not.",
